<title>SWITZERLAND: Winterthur confirms 1996 profit forecast.</title>
<headline>Winterthur confirms 1996 profit forecast.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Erwin Heri, chief financial officer for Winterthur Insurance Co, said the insurer was still expecting 1996 profits to rise by a double-digit amount, in line with the company's forecast.</p>
<p>&quot;We said we were expecting a double-digit growth in profits at the presentation of our half-year results in October. Nothing has changed since then,&quot; Heri told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;The prospects are actually even better,&quot; Heri added.</p>
<p>On October 1, 1996 Winterthur said good first half results formed a reliable basis on which full year profits should show a double-digit growth rate.</p>
<p>In 1995 Winterthur's group net profit rose 15.1 percent to 419.2 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
